1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,503
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:06,047
‪["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,383 --> 00:00:10,468
‪-<i>‪♪ Fix this</i>‪ ♪
‪-<i>‪♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i>‪ ♪

4
00:00:10,552 --> 00:00:12,762
‪♪ <i>‪Holding the scissors</i>‪ ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,182
‪♪ <i>‪One cut, and it's settled</i>‪ ♪

6
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:19,310
[Tonet] <i>I just want to correct</i>
<i>what Atoy knows!</i>

7
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:21,354
<i>You're toying with them!</i>

8
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:23,356
[Mongki] At last,
I can get back at you now!

9
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:24,524
PREVIOUSLY

10
00:00:24,607 --> 00:00:25,608
- [thumps, then thuds]
- [groans]

11
00:00:25,692 --> 00:00:26,818
- [whistle blowing]
- [guard] Stop!

12
00:00:27,485 --> 00:00:29,070
[clamoring]

13
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,490
[Martina, in English]
<i>It's better if you die.</i>

14
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:34,492
[in English] <i>I wish I could say</i>
<i>I'm sorry, but I'm not!</i>

15
00:00:36,202 --> 00:00:37,328
[Martina gasps]

16
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:41,791
[Ibyang] Tatoy, it's moving… Sister Tonet?

17
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:43,209
I have to say--

18
00:00:43,293 --> 00:00:45,128
Tonet, don't speak. I'll call for help.

19
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,383
Janine, she's not--

20
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:52,635
She's not…

21
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,220
[Ibyang] Sister Tonet, wake up!

22
00:00:54,304 --> 00:00:57,015
Wake up! [wails]

23
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:58,892
[woman] <i>Someone had</i>
<i>an accident. She might be dead!</i>

24
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:00,226
Atoy!

25
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,770
Bro, Tonet had an accident.

26
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:03,688
[Atoy] <i>She's the one</i>
<i>we put in the ambulance.</i>

27
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:04,731
- [ambulance siren wailing]
- Stop that!

28
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:06,399
My sister's inside!

29
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:07,567
Stop, stop!

30
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:09,652
[Emerson] <i>Netchai, Netchai.</i>

31
00:01:09,736 --> 00:01:11,362
[Cita sobbing] <i>Tonet didn't make it.</i>

32
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:13,531
<i>Emerson, she's gone.</i>

33
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,366
[shouting] She can't die!

34
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:17,577
She can't die, Miss Cita!

35
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:20,413
She can't be dead!

36
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:22,040
I was just with my sister!

37
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:25,335
- Emerson. She's gone.
- She was just there!

38
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:28,379
[sobbing and wailing]

39
00:01:28,463 --> 00:01:29,923
Emerson…

40
00:01:36,679 --> 00:01:38,389
It's confirmed. Tonet is dead.

41
00:01:39,057 --> 00:01:40,517
You can breathe now.

42
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,976
Don't worry, okay?

43
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:43,186
- [Cita] Let's go to her.
- I'll see you at home…

44
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:44,437
- Hey.
- [gasps]

45
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:46,981
Why are you hitting people? Are you blind?

46
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:49,484
You're the one who hit me.

47
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:51,277
[suspicious music playing]

48
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:52,445
You look familiar.

49
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:02,997
I know you.

50
00:02:03,706 --> 00:02:05,083
Red Regalia?

51
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:06,751
Ah…

52
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:10,296
You're the one
who threatened Atoy with a gun!

53
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:11,422
[scoffs]

54
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:13,133
It's useless anyway.

55
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:17,303
[sinister music playing]

56
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:19,472
What? Are you going to punch me?

57
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:21,641
Are you only tough against old women?

58
00:02:21,724 --> 00:02:22,851
Huh?

59
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:24,227
Mom.

60
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:25,979
Try it.

61
00:02:26,062 --> 00:02:27,856
Brother Atoy is going to finish you.

62
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:29,357
[music concludes]

63
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:32,235
[suave theme music playing]

64
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:11,441
Sis Ame, will Sis Tonet survive?

65
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,819
I'm worried.

66
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,446
When I held her,

67
00:03:16,529 --> 00:03:19,449
she closed her eyes and never woke up!

68
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:23,119
Maybe…

69
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:28,374
Tonet was just tired at that time.

70
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:30,960
But she's in the hospital now.

71
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:33,504
They won't neglect her there.

72
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:36,549
Maybe we can visit her tomorrow.

73
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:38,718
[somber music playing]

74
00:03:42,555 --> 00:03:44,140
- [Audrey] Hi.
- [Janine, in English] Mommy!

75
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:45,266
My child.

76
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:49,979
Atoy mentioned what happened.

77
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:52,357
How is Tonet?

78
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,525
[phone ringing]

79
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:56,236
I'll find out in a moment.

80
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:01,699
Hello, Miss Cita?

81
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:03,034
How is Tonet?

82
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:04,702
Is she okay?

83
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:20,927
All right.

84
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:23,513
Yes, Miss Cita. I'll take care of it.

85
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:25,974
Thank you.

86
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:43,324
Sis Ame, what did Miss Cita say?

87
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:46,202
Can we visit Sis Tonet?

88
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:58,923
Ibyang, don't think about that for now.

89
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:01,551
Just think…

90
00:05:06,889 --> 00:05:10,977
that Sister Tonet is happy
because you didn't leave her alone.

91
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,938
And also, she really loves you.

92
00:05:14,022 --> 00:05:14,856
Mm?

93
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:19,777
But Sis Ame, I already know that.

94
00:05:21,237 --> 00:05:26,367
And you're not answering my question.

95
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,084
Ibyang…

96
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:42,717
The doctors struggled
to treat Tonet's wounds.

97
00:05:44,093 --> 00:05:46,512
Her body couldn't take it anymore.

98
00:05:48,306 --> 00:05:50,892
We will never be with her again.

99
00:05:52,477 --> 00:05:53,811
She's gone.

100
00:05:56,355 --> 00:05:58,274
[melancholic music playing]

101
00:06:00,359 --> 00:06:01,486
[insudible]

102
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:07,867
[sobbing]

103
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:11,287
So… Sister Tonet is dead?

104
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:12,413
[sobs]

105
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:27,804
My Sister Tonet!

106
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:29,555
[wailing]

107
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:31,099
Sister Tonet…

108
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:35,978
Sister Tonet…

109
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:40,149
[in English] I'm so sorry, Ibyang.

110
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:42,860
Mommy, I want to go home.

111
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:44,654
[in English] Please?

112
00:06:47,865 --> 00:06:50,701
[Ibyang] Sister Tonet…

113
00:07:04,006 --> 00:07:06,050
[in English] Tonet, I'm sorry.

114
00:07:06,134 --> 00:07:10,263
If only I knew last night
was the last time we'd talk…

115
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:15,476
[sobbing]

116
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:19,480
Feeling giddy but with a question mark?

117
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:20,731
Is she trying to be trendy?

118
00:07:21,357 --> 00:07:23,401
Are you really in love or not?

119
00:07:23,901 --> 00:07:25,194
Or are you just leading him on?

120
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:30,616
Hey!

121
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:33,995
Girl, just ignore it.

122
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:36,581
You know what? Let's just eat siomai.

123
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:39,167
You go ahead. I don't feel like it.

124
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:41,002
[gentle music playing]

125
00:07:41,085 --> 00:07:42,378
Ah, tomorrow.

126
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:45,590
Come with me. I'll deliver
a suit to a client.

127
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:48,009
Then after that, let's get a foot spa.

128
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:49,594
[in English] Girly time!

129
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:52,597
I still have to help

130
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,725
at the blood donation drive tomorrow.
You go ahead.

131
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:59,854
After that? It's only half day, right?

132
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:02,565
You still don't want to?

133
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:05,067
[music fades]

134
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:09,363
- You!
- Give me that!

135
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:10,781
[gentle music playing]

136
00:08:13,743 --> 00:08:16,204
Remember this.

137
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:20,541
[in English] You need to enjoy
and live your life to the fullest!

138
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:23,461
Even if you know Gavin doesn't like you

139
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:25,588
and Cathy is the one he really wants.

140
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:27,840
Oh, be careful.

141
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:30,593
You might miss doing the things you want,

142
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:33,513
because you're always looking
for reasons to be mad at Cathy.

143
00:08:35,306 --> 00:08:36,807
There are things that

144
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:38,559
will never go your way.

145
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:44,315
Oh, whatever, Karla!

146
00:08:44,398 --> 00:08:47,485
I'll just leave. I'll eat siomai instead.

147
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:50,029
[in English] "To sio-mai love for you."

148
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,864
[laughs]

149
00:08:52,448 --> 00:08:53,407
Ha.

150
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:56,160
You really don't want to?

151
00:08:57,954 --> 00:08:59,330
[music fades]

152
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:00,998
[sobbing]

153
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:03,709
I should have gone with you.

154
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:07,004
I should have bonded with you.

155
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:10,174
- [sobbing continues]
- [melancholic music playing]

156
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:16,055
And I didn't grant your request.

157
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,727
[in English] I'm sorry, Tonet.

158
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:23,563
[melodramatic music playing]

159
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:27,525
[in English] I'm so sorry.

160
00:09:27,608 --> 00:09:30,319
[sobbing]

161
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:46,460
[music fades]

162
00:09:48,921 --> 00:09:52,717
Janine… My child, I'm so sorry.

163
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:55,428
I didn't know…

164
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:58,347
you were close to Tonet.

165
00:09:58,431 --> 00:10:01,392
Um, no. I wasn't close to her.

166
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:04,186
I just feel guilty.

167
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:07,523
Mm, Janine!

168
00:10:08,190 --> 00:10:09,775
Are you with Atoy?

169
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:10,860
[Janine] No.

170
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:12,903
Then who are you with?

171
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:14,447
None of your business.

172
00:10:15,072 --> 00:10:16,324
Janine!

173
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:20,494
I saw her in the mall restroom.
She was looking for Daddy.

174
00:10:20,578 --> 00:10:22,913
But I didn't say we were together.

175
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:24,624
- [heavy breathing]
- [pensive music playing]

176
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:28,419
I ran away because I didn't
want to be with her.

177
00:10:29,545 --> 00:10:31,213
She was on Ibyang's side.

178
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:34,091
[music fades]

179
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:36,469
Dear, I'm sorry.

180
00:10:36,552 --> 00:10:38,012
[somber music playing]

181
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:42,725
Why are you like that, Janine?

182
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:46,979
You should have brought Tonet to Tatoy.

183
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:52,026
Maybe nothing bad would've happened!

184
00:10:52,818 --> 00:10:53,819
Maybe she wouldn't have had the accident.

185
00:10:53,903 --> 00:10:55,905
Maybe she'd still be alive!

186
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:58,699
Ibyang… Oh, my dear…

187
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:01,994
Don't blame Janine.

188
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:06,374
I didn't know that would happen!

189
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:09,043
Don't pick a fight with me!

190
00:11:09,126 --> 00:11:11,337
I'll fight you…

191
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:14,340
because you're really bad!

192
00:11:14,423 --> 00:11:15,716
[sobs]

193
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,803
[Audrey] Ibyang. Ibyang, listen to me.

194
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:21,847
- [sobbing]
- I know this is painful you.

195
00:11:23,891 --> 00:11:26,394
But Janine didn't want

196
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:28,896
for Tonet to die.

197
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:33,984
No, but she's really bad!

198
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:35,778
[sobbing]

199
00:11:35,861 --> 00:11:37,405
Because of you…

200
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:41,909
I lost someone…

201
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:45,413
who loved me!

202
00:11:45,496 --> 00:11:47,331
[sobbing]

203
00:11:49,708 --> 00:11:51,001
Because of you!

204
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:56,382
You always want to be the star!

205
00:11:56,465 --> 00:11:59,802
[sobbing]

206
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:03,013
What more do you want, Janine? [sobbing]

207
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:08,894
You have a mother. You have a father!

208
00:12:10,104 --> 00:12:13,023
Isn't that enough for you? [sobs]

209
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:17,278
You're so selfish!

210
00:12:17,361 --> 00:12:20,281
[sobbing]

211
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:25,619
[melodramatic music playing]

212
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:57,860
Rest now, Netchai.

213
00:12:57,943 --> 00:12:59,737
[somber music playing]

214
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:01,864
Thank you for showing yourself to me.

215
00:13:03,949 --> 00:13:06,076
You still made me feel your love.

216
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:23,344
- [melancholic music playing]
- [clicks tongue]

217
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:34,688
[sighs]

218
00:13:34,772 --> 00:13:36,482
- [Atoy] What's the news, 'Son?
- [Cita sobs]

219
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:40,694
What did the police and the admin say?

220
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:44,532
- I spoke to them, but…
- [Cita sobs]

221
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:45,741
[sniffles, clicks tongue]

222
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:50,579
I couldn't understand
what they said about Tonet's death.

223
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:53,624
- A "freak accident"?
- [Cita sobs]

224
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:58,462
She… She was just hit
by some scaffolding, like that?

225
00:13:59,463 --> 00:14:02,633
[Cita] Well, according to a witness,

226
00:14:02,716 --> 00:14:06,011
there was a man forcing her
to go with him because…

227
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:08,138
he accused her of stealing something.

228
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:10,266
[stammers]

229
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:12,393
So Tonet ran, because she denied it.

230
00:14:12,476 --> 00:14:13,978
She never did that.

231
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:16,397
He tried to drag her to the precinct.

232
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:18,566
Maybe security chased her,

233
00:14:18,649 --> 00:14:20,943
and that's how she ended up

234
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:23,112
in that vacant area under construction.

235
00:14:23,195 --> 00:14:26,240
- Impossible. That's impossible.
- [Cita sniffles]

236
00:14:26,323 --> 00:14:28,325
- My sister would never steal.
- [Cita inhales]

237
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:34,915
Who was the man accusing her of theft?

238
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:38,127
[rousing music playing]

239
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:45,092
[mysterious music playing]

240
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:46,427
Martina.

241
00:14:47,928 --> 00:14:50,723
The maid told me you've been
drinking since you got here.

242
00:14:51,473 --> 00:14:52,892
What's your problem?

243
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:54,393
Tonet is dead.

244
00:14:54,476 --> 00:14:57,104
[in English] I just need to unwind
and get outside of my mind.

245
00:14:57,187 --> 00:14:58,564
[in English] Jeez.

246
00:14:58,647 --> 00:15:00,316
That's your second bottle!

247
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:03,485
Wasn't that enough to unwind?

248
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:06,030
[in English] I know what you're saying.

249
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:09,241
But I can't get her face
out of my mind. Okay?

250
00:15:09,325 --> 00:15:10,743
It's the first time I killed someone.

251
00:15:10,826 --> 00:15:11,952
[in English] I've never done that!

252
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:15,122
[in English] I feel sick to my stomach
just thinking about it.

253
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:16,624
[sighs]

254
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:18,375
[in English] Just let me freaking drink.

255
00:15:18,459 --> 00:15:19,376
[in English] Okay.

256
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:21,837
If that calms you down,

257
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:22,922
go ahead, get drunk.

258
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:24,548
[music intensifies]

259
00:15:25,132 --> 00:15:28,344
But you killed her for a good reason.

260
00:15:29,261 --> 00:15:32,097
If Tonet were alive, we'd be ruined.

261
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:34,600
[in English] So, relax.

262
00:15:35,559 --> 00:15:36,560
[in English] I'm proud of you.

263
00:15:37,144 --> 00:15:38,312
[in English] Okay?

264
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:44,777
[in English] Wanna sip?

265
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:58,791
[music fades]

266
00:15:58,874 --> 00:16:04,129
[Mercado] <i>I emailed</i>
<i>the CV of SPO3 Miguel Reyes.</i>

267
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:06,423
What's this for, Padua?

268
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:07,675
Just a personal mission, sir.

269
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:12,137
My assistant at the shop, Tonet…

270
00:16:12,846 --> 00:16:14,098
She died, sir.

271
00:16:15,015 --> 00:16:16,225
I suspect

272
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:18,560
it wasn't an accident.

273
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:23,732
This SPO3 Miguel Reyes…

274
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:28,487
I researched. He's the officer
assigned to this case.

275
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:29,947
Ah.

276
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:33,075
So, you're going to be a cop now?

277
00:16:33,158 --> 00:16:35,411
You'll need an ID and a badge.

278
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:37,079
I can't produce those.

279
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:39,790
I don't need a real ID and badge, Colonel.

280
00:16:41,291 --> 00:16:43,627
[rock music playing]

281
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:44,586
[Mercado chuckles softly]

282
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:46,839
Looks like you're prepared.

283
00:16:46,922 --> 00:16:47,840
[in English] Good luck, Padua.

284
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:49,133
[Atoy, in English] <i>Thank you, sir.</i>

285
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:53,303
[music swells]

286
00:16:57,391 --> 00:17:00,894
[device blipping]

287
00:17:37,556 --> 00:17:39,224
Wait a moment, okay.
I'll just go to the restroom.

288
00:17:48,942 --> 00:17:50,027
[phone ringing]

289
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:56,867
[line ringing]

290
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:11,131
[voice recording, in English]
<i>I'm sorry, all circuits are--</i>

291
00:18:13,217 --> 00:18:15,052
[T-Bak] Hey, Karla!

292
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:17,554
Karla.

293
00:18:17,638 --> 00:18:19,598
We heard what happened to Tonet.

294
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:25,020
Yes, she's gone.

295
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:27,314
She had an accident.

296
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:31,193
[in English] I'm so sorry, Karla.

297
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:38,158
Let me hug you too.

298
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:44,623
Thank you for being here.

299
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:49,962
Even if I didn't call you,
you're here for me.

300
00:18:50,045 --> 00:18:51,755
Of course.

301
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:53,799
We're your best friends, right?

302
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:55,384
We won't leave you.

303
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:56,510
We'll be with you through everything.

304
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:59,138
And Karla, this is for life.

305
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,055
Come on.

306
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,682
We're your backup
and support in everything.

307
00:19:01,765 --> 00:19:02,808
That's correct!

308
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:06,520
[in English] Does… Does Gavin know?

309
00:19:06,603 --> 00:19:08,105
[in English] He's with Cathy.

310
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:10,357
[in English] I'll call him right now.

311
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:12,151
Ah, no, don't.

312
00:19:12,776 --> 00:19:16,446
I don't want you to disturb
their date with my bad news.

313
00:19:17,197 --> 00:19:18,824
Just let him be.

314
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:21,535
[somber music playing]

315
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:34,464
[music fades]

316
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:36,758
Uh, Officer Reyes, good evening.

317
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:38,135
- What do you need?
- [in English] Good evening.

318
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:43,682
I'm investigating what happened
to, um… Tonet, Tonet Mendoza.

319
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:46,059
I gathered that

320
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:50,147
she was accused of stealing
before she died.

321
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:52,774
What item was she supposed to have stolen?

322
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:55,861
Sir, nothing specific was mentioned.

323
00:19:55,944 --> 00:19:58,572
But there were two victims.

324
00:19:58,655 --> 00:20:00,657
One woman said it was a cell phone.

325
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:02,868
Cell phone?

326
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:04,745
[suspicious music playing]

327
00:20:04,828 --> 00:20:07,539
But no cell phone was found
among her things,

328
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,333
except her own.

329
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:13,754
Maybe she threw it away
while she was running.

330
00:20:13,837 --> 00:20:15,464
You know how thieves are

331
00:20:15,547 --> 00:20:16,965
when they're about to be caught.

332
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:21,261
It's strange, because Tonet
had no police record.

333
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:24,181
So, it looks like
she really wasn't a thief.

334
00:20:25,307 --> 00:20:30,520
It also said she worked
at a tailoring shop in Baclaran.

335
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:33,732
So, she had a job. She seemed decent.

336
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:35,317
And she wasn't part of any gang.

337
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:37,069
She wasn't on the gang list.

338
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:38,612
So…

339
00:20:38,695 --> 00:20:40,697
When I spoke to her brother,

340
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:46,328
he said she went to the mall to meet him.

341
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:52,668
So, what did the man and woman
who accused her look like?

342
00:20:53,168 --> 00:20:57,089
Sir, the man was tall, fair-skinned.

343
00:20:57,172 --> 00:20:58,590
The way he dressed, he looked rich!

344
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:02,970
And the woman was beautiful, round eyes.

345
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:05,806
I can't forget what Tonet said,

346
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:09,017
that they seemed like accomplices.

347
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:10,477
She said they were husband and wife.

348
00:21:11,603 --> 00:21:13,105
A husband and wife, you say?

349
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:20,654
[tense music playing]

350
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:23,115
This CCTV of yours?

351
00:21:24,449 --> 00:21:25,867
Can I see it?

352
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:30,289
Sir, our computer system crashed
during the fire alarm.

353
00:21:30,372 --> 00:21:33,750
All the recorded files
from that day were erased.

354
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:36,253
So, we don't have any footage.

355
00:21:36,336 --> 00:21:38,255
- Erased?
- [in English] Yes, sir.

356
00:21:38,338 --> 00:21:39,923
How could it be erased?

357
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:41,758
[music intensifies]

358
00:21:43,093 --> 00:21:44,803
Unless someone erased it.

359
00:21:44,886 --> 00:21:47,180
[music swells]

360
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:54,313
[suspicious music playing]

361
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:43,028
[music swells]

362
00:22:59,294 --> 00:23:00,962
Expensive perfume.

363
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:02,214
[music fades]

364
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:06,426
This isn't the perfume Tonet wore.

365
00:23:06,968 --> 00:23:11,973
[tense music playing]

366
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:15,560
[music fades]

367
00:23:18,146 --> 00:23:19,397
[Audrey groans]

368
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:22,943
[in English] Say that again, Audrey.

369
00:23:23,026 --> 00:23:25,946
Janine saw Tonet… die?

370
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:27,739
[in English] I'm not sure.

371
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:29,574
But she saw Tonet's condition

372
00:23:29,658 --> 00:23:31,660
when she had the accident inside the mall.

373
00:23:32,869 --> 00:23:34,037
What she said…

374
00:23:35,622 --> 00:23:36,790
she was covered in blood.

375
00:23:37,624 --> 00:23:41,211
[in English] Oh, uh, that must be
traumatizing for her.

376
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:44,714
Uh, but why did Atoy
even bring the child there?

377
00:23:45,423 --> 00:23:47,676
He didn't mean to, Dad.

378
00:23:48,969 --> 00:23:51,054
[in English] It's just…
It's just all so sudden.

379
00:23:51,138 --> 00:23:54,599
This morning, Tonet was here
to see me, and now…

380
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:56,726
she's gone.

381
00:23:57,853 --> 00:24:01,439
[in English] Well, I mean,
that's life, right, Audrey?

382
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:04,609
We never really know when we'll be taken.

383
00:24:04,693 --> 00:24:06,444
And, Audrey, please

384
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:09,531
don't let Janine sleep
at her father's house.

385
00:24:09,614 --> 00:24:11,575
[in English] It doesn't seem
like she's safe with him.

386
00:24:11,658 --> 00:24:13,952
You don't know Atoy.

387
00:24:14,911 --> 00:24:17,414
Wow! Now you're defending him?

388
00:24:18,498 --> 00:24:21,168
[suspicious music playing]

389
00:24:26,298 --> 00:24:28,049
[in English] Wait. Uh, Martina…

390
00:24:30,468 --> 00:24:31,761
Have you been drinking?

391
00:24:31,845 --> 00:24:34,014
[in English] Yes. Sorry, Dad. Just, uh…

392
00:24:34,097 --> 00:24:36,766
[in English] Um, trying
to wind down a little bit.

393
00:24:36,850 --> 00:24:38,602
Uh, I'm a little bit tipsy.
I'm not used to it anymore.

394
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:40,353
[in English] So, I think I'm just gonna…

395
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:42,189
[Dmitri, in English]
Wait. What happened to your bag?

396
00:24:42,272 --> 00:24:44,024
[in English] It's missing a stud. Look.

397
00:24:44,524 --> 00:24:45,400
There, see?

398
00:24:45,483 --> 00:24:46,318
[in English] Oh.

399
00:24:48,195 --> 00:24:49,821
I just noticed it now.

400
00:24:50,530 --> 00:24:51,865
- Where did you go the whole day?
- [Martina mutters]

401
00:24:51,948 --> 00:24:53,909
- [suspicious music playing]
- [dramatic stinging]

402
00:25:07,672 --> 00:25:10,967
- [dramatic sting]
- [tense music playing]

403
00:25:21,144 --> 00:25:21,978
‪[electronic blipping]

404
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:34,699
Ah, sorry…

405
00:25:34,783 --> 00:25:36,326
I just got distracted by your bag.

406
00:25:36,409 --> 00:25:37,410
[in English] Oh, thank you!

407
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,996
[in English] It's my favorite one!
My lucky bag.

408
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:44,501
But it seems… something's missing,
a little broken.

409
00:25:44,584 --> 00:25:48,421
Like it's missing a stud. Just like… this?

410
00:25:48,505 --> 00:25:49,381
UP NEXT

411
00:25:49,464 --> 00:25:52,300
There's evidence. We need to divert it.

412
00:25:52,384 --> 00:25:55,804
Find out if Emerson
will file a case against his wife.

413
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:58,723
If Emerson pushes through
with his complaint,

414
00:25:59,724 --> 00:26:00,725
what will happen to him?

415
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:03,770
Maybe Emerson will be next.
He'll end up like his sister.

416
00:26:03,853 --> 00:26:07,065
The mother of your child…
She's part of the Regalia family.

417
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:08,650
If things get tough,

418
00:26:08,733 --> 00:26:10,443
whose side will you take?

419
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:12,612
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

420
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:15,740
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

421
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:17,409
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

422
00:26:17,492 --> 00:26:18,660
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
